Overlay patch 0045 (D-052; reference D-082 / Shipwright-ios ff0d0e8 overlay 0063):
GYRO AIMING FROM THE PHONE'S OWN SENSOR.

Upstream 2S2H already aims with gyro: Ship_HandleFirstPersonAiming
(z_player.c; bow, hookshot, Deku bubble, Tatl/C-up first-person view) adds
gyro_y*720 to focus.rot.y and -gyro_x*720 to focus.rot.x per tick from the
N64 pad's gyro fields, gated by its own
gEnhancements.Camera.FirstPerson.GyroEnabled. LUS fills those fields only from
an SDL gamepad gyro mapping, which an iPhone has none of. The shell
(app/ios/SohIosShell.m) runs CoreMotion while the iOS setting "Gyro Aiming"
(gSohIos.Gyro) is on and hands out SDLGyroMapping-shaped samples (gyro_x =
pitch, gyro_y = yaw, rad/s x sensitivity -- the same FIELD semantics as SoH;
2S2H only names its locals the other way round); this patch copies them into
port 1's pad. __IOS__-gated; the desktop build is unchanged.

  1. padmgr.c PadMgr_UpdateInputs, port 1 (i == 0), after the D-pad masking
     (outside overlay 0044's hunk AND its 3-line context, so both patches stay
     independently reversible): when SohIos_GyroActive() (setting on AND
     CoreMotion running or a bridge `gyro` injection live), overwrite
     input->cur.gyro_x/gyro_y with SohIos_GyroSample. With the setting off
     nothing is touched, so a physical controller's own LUS gyro mapping keeps
     working. Only the first-person aim reads these fields, so the free /
     third-person camera is unaffected (reference spec).

  2. padmgr.c, end of file: SohIos_PlayerFocusRot, a read-only instrument for
     the console bridge's `gyro` command (Link's focus.rot = the aim), so the
     sim round can prove an injected rate moved the aim.

Generate against a vendor tree with 0001..0044 applied and 0045 not applied.


--- a/mm/src/code/padmgr.c
+++ b/mm/src/code/padmgr.c
@@ -516,6 +516,21 @@
             input->cur.button &= ~(BTN_DRIGHT | BTN_DLEFT);
         }
 
+#ifdef __IOS__
+        /* SOH_IOS (overlay 0045, D-052): "Gyro Aiming" -- the phone's
+         * CoreMotion rates (SDLGyroMapping units: pitch/yaw rad/s x
+         * sensitivity) drive z_player's first-person gyro aim. Only while the
+         * iOS setting is on, so a pad's LUS gyro mapping still works when it
+         * is off. */
+        if (i == 0) {
+            extern int SohIos_GyroActive(void);
+            extern void SohIos_GyroSample(float* x, float* y);
+            if (SohIos_GyroActive()) {
+                SohIos_GyroSample(&input->cur.gyro_x, &input->cur.gyro_y);
+            }
+        }
+#endif
+
         // Calculate pressed and relative inputs
         diff = input->prev.button ^ input->cur.button;
         input->press.button |= (u16)(diff & input->cur.button);
@@ -832,4 +847,23 @@
 
     // osCreateThread(&sPadMgrInstance->thread, threadId, PadMgr_ThreadEntry, sPadMgrInstance, stack, pri);
     // osStartThread(&sPadMgrInstance->thread);
+}
+
+#ifdef __IOS__
+/* SOH_IOS (overlay 0045, D-052): console `gyro` instrument -- Link's aim
+ * (focus.rot x/y). Read-only; returns 0 outside gameplay. */
+int SohIos_PlayerFocusRot(int* x, int* y) {
+    extern PlayState* gPlayState;
+    Player* player;
+    if (gPlayState == NULL) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    player = GET_PLAYER(gPlayState);
+    if (player == NULL) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    *x = player->actor.focus.rot.x;
+    *y = player->actor.focus.rot.y;
+    return 1;
 }
+#endif
